     domain/CustomerSort.java          a sort instruction the repository understands
     service/CustomerService.java      what the UI talks to
     ui/CustomerListView.java          the view at /
 ```

+## Filtering
+
+The list can be narrowed by name and by status. Both filters are applied by
+`CustomerRepository`, so the grid still holds one page of rows at a time and the
+row count still comes from a count query — a filtered list costs one count query
+and one page query, no matter how large the data set is.
+
+The filter is part of the URL, as the query parameters `name` and `status`
+(comma separated, in declaration order): `/?name=vir&status=ACTIVE,CLOSED`.
+Opening such a URL applies the filter and fills in the two fields; changing a
+filter replaces the current history entry rather than pushing a new one, so
+typing does not fill up the back button. Name matching ignores case and accents
+in both directions, and every whitespace-separated term has to occur in the
+first or the last name.
+
 The 500 customers live in `src/main/resources/customers.csv` and are loaded once
 at startup.

